# /em — a standing EM, on demand, in its own window

The model (Chris, 2026-10-31): each Engineering Manager is `claude --name <repo>-standing`
in one tmux pane, one per repo, shown in its own maximized Ghostty titled
`<repo> — standing EM`. The Director starts an EM the first time it needs one, never all
at init, opens its window so Chris can watch the work alongside the Director's, and Chris
closes windows at will to tidy his workspace: closing a terminal only detaches a tmux
client, the session keeps running. Canon: `~/repos/lentago/CLAUDE.md` § Director init and
§ Dispatch protocol.

## Forms

| Invocation | Does |
|---|---|
| `/em status` | which EMs are up (`ListAgents` + `standing status`), which have a window |
| `/em <repo>` | ensure the EM is up, open its window |
| `/em show <repo>` | open its window (idempotent) |
| `/em hide <repo>` | close its window(s); the session keeps running |
| `/em <repo> <ask…>` | ensure up, open window, dispatch the ask, report in one line |
| `/em down <repo>` | end the EM with `standing down <repo>`; only when Chris asked or its work is closed and he agreed |

## Procedure

1. **Status.** `ListAgents`: is `<repo>-standing` listed? `standing status` gives one row
   per EM: state, pid, and in TERM how many terminals show it (`none` = no window).
2. **Start if absent, one at a time** (two concurrent starts can race, kalmia#247):

   ```
   standing up <repo> --director <your session name>
   ```

   While the tmux session `lentago-director` exists (Chris starts it with `director`),
   `--director` defaults to `lentago-director`; pass it when you run under any other name.
   `up` opens a terminal for the EM it starts, and only for that one. Then check
   `ListAgents` every 10 s, up to 60 s, until the name appears. If `standing status`
   shows `trust?`, stop and tell Chris: accepting the folder-trust dialog is his
   (`standing trust`).
3. **Show** an EM that was already up: `standing show <repo>`. It opens one terminal,
   or says the EM is already shown and opens nothing. Never `standing open`: it reopens
   every EM's window, including ones Chris closed.
4. **Dispatch** per the protocol: `SendMessage` to `<repo>-standing` with
   `notify_when_idle: true`; first line is the ask in one sentence; carry the issue number
   (file it first), the deliverable, what is out of scope, any judgment already decided.
   One ask per message.
5. **Report** to Chris in one line: started or already up, window opened, what was
   dispatched. Then carry on; the EM's reply and the idle notice arrive on their own.
6. **Hide** on request: `standing hide <repo>` closes its terminal(s); the EM keeps
   running and `standing show <repo>` brings the window back.

## Don'ts

- No bare `standing up` (it starts every repo) and no parallel `standing up`.
- No polling `ListAgents` for a reply; wait for the EM's message or the idle notice.
- If the classifier blocks `standing up` or `trust`, route it to Chris, never to an EM.
- Don't edit inside a repo that has a live EM; hand off (`~/.claude/CLAUDE.md`).
